  "knowledgePattern": "Subtract neighbouring partial-sum recurrences before summing reciprocal terms",
  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Compare neighbouring definitions",
      "body": "<p>Write the given sum rule for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></math> and for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></math>. Subtract the equations so that all their shared terms cancel.</p>",
      "recap": "Subtracting overlapping sums leaves only the terms that occur in one sum.",
      "pitfall": "Check the starting term separately; the rule for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></math> starts at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>.",
      "pause": "Find how <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></math> is related to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></math> and calculate the first term used in the requested series.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l08",
          "reminder": "Subtracting overlapping sums leaves only the terms that occur in one sum."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Build the series being asked for",
      "body": "<p>Use the relation between neighbouring terms to simplify <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>. Work out its first term and common ratio.</p>",
      "recap": "A geometric series sums to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math> when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>.",
      "pitfall": "The sum starts at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>; it does not include <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></math> in a denominator.",
      "pause": "Check convergence and calculate the infinite sum.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l09",
          "reminder": "A geometric series sums to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math> when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "solution": "<p><strong>1.</strong> The initial recurrence gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>. For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x02265;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>, write the definition at n+1 and n, then subtract: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></math>. Therefore <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></math> for these indices.</p><p><strong>2.</strong> Thus <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x02265;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>. In particular, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x000B7;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math> for the terms used in the requested sum.</p><p><strong>3.</strong> The reciprocal series has first term <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math> and common ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>, so its sum is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></math>. Answer B. The initial step from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></math> has a different ratio and is not part of this reciprocal series.</p>"
}
